sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Doctor as Doctor (Clinician)
    participant Client as Web Client (React)
    participant Server as Backend API Gateway
    participant Safety as Medicine Safety Engine
    participant DB as MongoDB Atlas
    actor Pharmacist as Pharmacy Staff
    actor Patient as Patient

    Doctor->>Client: Enters symptoms & patient NIC
    Client->>Server: POST /api/doctors/predict-disease (symptoms)
    Server-->>Client: Suggestions (Tier 1 curated / Tier 2 KB)
    Doctor->>Client: Selects diagnosis & prescribes drugs
    Client->>Server: POST /api/doctors/consultations
    Server->>Safety: checkSafety(drugs, dosages, duration)
    Safety-->>Server: Dosage verified / Warning flagged
    Server->>DB: Encrypt & insert Consultation (AES-256-GCM)
    Server->>DB: Insert Prescription (Status: 'pending')
    Server-->>Client: Consultation saved + Prescription issued

    Patient->>Pharmacist: Presents patient NIC / prescription ID
    Pharmacist->>Client: Searches pending prescriptions by NIC
    Client->>Server: GET /api/prescriptions/search?nic=...
    Server->>DB: Lookup via patientNic_bi (Blind Index)
    DB-->>Server: Decrypted prescription records
    Server-->>Client: Pending prescription lines
    Pharmacist->>Client: Dispenses drugs (or inputs brand alternative)
    Client->>Server: POST /api/prescriptions/dispense
    Server->>DB: Atomically update Prescription (Status: 'dispensed')
    Server->>DB: Insert Dispensing audit record
    Server-->>Client: Dispensing confirmed & inventory decremented
